-- EverlookDB Auctions: gear upgrades. What a piece of gear is worth to your spec, and whether it beats what you wear.
--   Specs     each character gears for one or more specs of its class ("not sure yet": several), picked once when
--             the auction house or the Upgrades window first opens, later on the Gear upgrades settings page or
--             with /eah up spec <name>
--   Weights   per spec, built in (UpgradesData.lua, generated by tools/gen_upgrades.py from wowsims/forever, MIT):
--             what one point of each stat is worth, optionally adjusted to the character's talents. A profile of
--             your own copies them and lets you change any value; strings import and export (ours and Pawn's)
--   Score     every stat the game reports for an item version (random suffixes too) times the weights, plus the
--             average value of procs and Use: effects (optional), against what is worn in that slot: rings and
--             trinkets against the weaker of the two, an off-hand against a two-handed weapon, an empty slot filled
--   Upgrades  the last full scan (our own or the shared one from the EverlookDB App), read in small batches over
--             frames and never in combat: the best upgrade per slot within the max price (UpgradesTab.lua)
-- Tooltips, bag badges, quest rewards and grey items at vendors are in UpgradesExtras.lua; the settings page in
-- UpgradesOptions.lua. Nothing about other players is read or saved.
local ADDON, ns = ...

local U = {}
ns.up = U

local function data() return ns.UP_DATA or { classes = {}, procs = {}, ratings = {} } end

